cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pyflightstream, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "pyflightstream: version-aware, didactic Python driver for the FlightStream panel-method solver"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Neves
    given-names: Geovana
license: MIT
# The version and the release date are set together, always. Between
# releases this file carries a development version and NO date-released,
# because a development tree has no release date; it once stated the
# v0.3.0 date beside version 0.4.0.dev0, so a citation generated from
# that tree asserted a release date for an artifact that was never
# released (REV010-015). This is a RELEASE tree: the version carries no
# .dev0 and the release date is set beside it, which is the pair the
# guard in tests/test_metadata_currency.py enforces in both directions.
# The older archive DOIs below stay, because those releases did happen
# and are still what a citation of them should resolve to.
version: 0.5.0
date-released: 2026-08-09
repository-code: "https://github.com/nevesgeovana/pyflightstream"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21795265
    description: "Zenodo archive of release v0.4.0"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21515614
    description: "Zenodo archive of release v0.3.0"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21482924
    description: "Zenodo concept DOI (resolves to the latest version)"
abstract: >-
  Version-aware Python driver for the FlightStream panel-method
  solver: a command database with per-version evidence statuses backed
  by committed probe reports, a validating script builder, managed
  campaign execution, anchor-based output parsers, a three-tier QA
  harness with banded physics references and cross-version drift
  checks, far-field probe surveys with conservation ledgers, and a
  fluid-structure interaction subpackage coupling a rotating-blade
  beam model to the solver's aeroelastic toolbox.
keywords:
  - aerodynamics
  - panel method
  - FlightStream
  - aeroelasticity
  - propeller
  - solver automation
  - verification and validation
